# GMS's aura is an active: 100 HP, up for 70 + 2x seconds on a 120-second wait.
# The wait is shorter than the duration at every level, so a player who presses
# it holds it permanently -- which is what a passive is. The HP cost goes with
# the cast that no longer happens.
#
# Both levers are x/5 in GMS, one floored and one ceiled: 10 + floor(x/5)% of
# defence ignored and ceil(x/5)% final damage. Written straight, without the
# rounding, that is a fifth of a point a level on each -- so master lands on
# GMS's 16% and 6% exactly and only where they start moves.
#
# The wave is 500 + 20x%, six lines on ten enemies, on its own five-second
# clock. GMS makes as many waves as the triggering skill has lines and pays a
# share of that skill's damage; a flat wave on a clock is the same skill from
# the fight's side, since a warrior at 5th job is always swinging something.
name: "Weapon Aura"
description:
  "Infuses your weapon with a portion of your health, granting it a visible "
  "aura and empowering it."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_HERO_V skill_order: 1 }
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_PALADIN_V skill_order: 1 }
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_DARK_KNIGHT_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_ARCHETYPE
max_level: 30
base {
  ied_pct: 0.102
  final_dmg_pct: 0.002
}
per_level {
  ied_pct: 0.002
  final_dmg_pct: 0.002
}
auto_mode {
  label: "Aura Wave"
  cast_interval_seconds: 5.0
  max_enemies: 10
  lines: 6
  base { skill_pct: 5.20 }
  per_level { skill_pct: 0.20 }
}
